// path - which is what produces the error the two engines share.
// ---- complex arithmetic, as CPython 3.14's Objects/complexobject.c ----
//
// Each answer is a [real, imag] pair. CPython's binary is compiled with
// floating-point contraction, so every `x + y * z` in its C source is a fused
// multiply-add and the last bit of a quotient or a general power depends on it;
// pyCxFma is that fused operation. Twin of the pyCx* functions in
// abnf/jsrt.go.

// fma(a, b, c): a*b + c rounded ONCE. Dekker's exact product and Knuth's exact
// sum carry the value as s + v + w; rounding s + v is the answer unless s + v
// is exactly halfway between two doubles, where w decides. Outside the range
